* ''The channel of intent'' (operator, 2026-10-20: //"Approve your leans, land the full models into the architecture now"//). The daemon wiki keeps working memory; a face's intents travel on that face's own intent plane, `@intents-<tag>`, a fifth face plane beside the four; a vessel's own records rest in its daemon bag, unmirrored; the face's pins rest in the face's custody and `@persona`. The approved leans: the plane stands from the first landing, never staged in the daemon bag; the winner reads by the intent's own preference list, else the lowest `H(atom ‖ intent id)`, and never elects; a single-effect fleet-wide verb never addresses "any device", and a human answer may name its executor; a claim never expires, a device's staleness stays a local suspicion, and the operator's release always wins; an `every` intent reaches a later-joined device unless its bound names a roster edge; a far agent reaches the plane through a relay seat, opt-in per face and ring-gated, its research before its build; an intent voids by supersession, a revoked delegation, a passed roster edge or the operator's cancel; compaction folds by the operator's act, never a timer; a local verb that touches its own vessel alone bypasses the plane and leaves its receipt in that vessel's bag. The plane carries a hand's decisions that cross devices, never its motion (the rubric, <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane`>> #/the-rubric). Item `I1`.

